  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Co-creating Peace: Participation of Diverse Young Women in the Urban-Rural and Indigenous Civic Space in Nari&#xf1;o and Cauca</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is based on the previous experience of UN Women and the International Organization for Migration (IOM) in strengthening processes of youth participation and empowerment of young women in Nari&#xf1;o and Cauca, Colombia, through processes aimed at participation in the implementation of the Peace Agreement (2016). The project promotes the participation and influence of young urban, rural, indigenous and Afro-Colombian women in civic spaces for peacebuilding, transforming conflicts in Pasto and Ricaurte - Department of Nari&#xf1;o, and Popay&#xe1;n and Santander de Quilichao - Department of Cauca. Through the co-creation of innovative initiatives for the care of civic space, citizen participation and peacebuilding, young women will be protagonists in the identification and solution of their needs, introducing innovative elements to civic space and social mobilisation, as well as the exchange of knowledge and experiences of conflict management and conflict resolution through culture, based on their own forms of organisation, participation, communication, cultural and artistic expressions.</narrative>
  </description>
